# Authentication for the agents. Set ONE of the two.
#
# Sandcastle forwards every key declared in .sandcastle/.env into the sandbox,
# taking the value from this file and falling back to your shell environment for
# any key left blank. Nothing here is hardcoded to an API key — either works.

# Option A — use your Claude subscription. Run `claude setup-token` on your host
# and paste the token here. Consumes no API credits.
# Background: https://github.com/mattpocock/sandcastle/issues/191
CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=

# Option B — use a metered Anthropic API key instead.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# GitHub personal access token — the agent uses it to read and manage GitHub Issues.
# Fine-grained token needs Issues (Read and write) + Metadata (Read):
# https://github.com/settings/personal-access-tokens/new
# Or simply reuse the gh CLI's own token: `gh auth token`.
GH_TOKEN=
